{"title":"2019 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 4b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2019 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <i>Shonk sequence</i> is a sequence of positive integers in which\n</p>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: circle;\">\n<li>each term after the first is greater than the previous term, and</li>\n<li>the product of all terms is a perfect square.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For example: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/e/8ee67283c870532df36c30af9a1f939be31b4e1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 6, 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> is a Shonk sequence since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d9211bff6cd63555f615900e9b1fefcd83f03328.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8f91e00ae6daeb0e897185b67ab794418e04755.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27 &gt; 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/3/aa371e0e900504e502e131938cbaffc5a897bb99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 6 \\times 27 = 324 = 18^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/a/b1a94cc82589bf45ea163a9b24c38d7868fe264e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12, x, 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"17\" /> is a Shonk sequence, what is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/1/131f0ae0f974b7d6eee98c0dfd23e73b2bc4ea18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2} \\times 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> and the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/9/339baf6df71777af266e6259546917b0742caf2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b5576de83ff1ee569e0a1f3b24db57252b9a38be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, since the product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/9/339baf6df71777af266e6259546917b0742caf2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> has to be a perfect square, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d379b13c2338ee58a27252096b2544c9e8e37c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$yz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"11\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/8/e38baca0cab3a1f16069f2793b2c3a40faf434bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 7 \\times 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" /> times some perfect square.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> because if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are prime, they wouldn't be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> based on the prime factorization, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b5576de83ff1ee569e0a1f3b24db57252b9a38be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/b/9db5fe3b260c1a3353ffb62756aaa746a9d3487f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\times 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> are both greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/9/339baf6df71777af266e6259546917b0742caf2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>However, the only multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> that is <i>not</i> greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/9/339baf6df71777af266e6259546917b0742caf2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/e/bee536bc056a88630472c3cb881a52887e3057d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f003341b99f4cdc86cd566488c951397895827f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, this means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/4/1a4f5d3af682cf2576ec0757ea1501c25a74debe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{y = 35}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"29\" /> because the only multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> but below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/9/339baf6df71777af266e6259546917b0742caf2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e058d401a1b942f106f081ff1fcca8a8b1d42a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1d1611143f5792dc0f61f3b130af88cb790c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, which are greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times some perfect square and be either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e058d401a1b942f106f081ff1fcca8a8b1d42a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1d1611143f5792dc0f61f3b130af88cb790c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/5/d7514f874de361fd750640826acd73989d823d66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52 = 2^{2} \\times 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a66ca2216d6e3ae3ff41ef3a11c3d6ac2c54809.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39 = 3 \\times 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/c/84c58bf042dd196a988ac29db7108a1e5dd1a0eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{z = 12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"65\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018011049\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.033 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 153/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 499/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7889/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.856      1 2019_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4\n100.00%    6.856      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36930:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018011049 and revision id 285736. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}